title: Caravan rendering layer
---
[root] Backend-neutral rendering slice (notstarted)
Build the first concrete rendering layer on top of the completed indexed anchor. Keep this packet small: it should make a deterministic, inspectable render value from one immutable `GameState<Snapshot>` and one `Tau` through the existing engine-presentation boundary. It is a render-model and demo slice, not a final graphics architecture.
Files: rendering.vine; spec/initial.md; proposals/productization-review.md; proposals/stage-layer.md; proposals/input-and-interaction.md; roadmap.md; crates/engine-presentation/**; crates/caravan-demo/**
Do: Dispatch the contract, projection, demo wiring, and evidence tasks only after their dependencies are reviewed. Preserve the distinction between authoritative game state and owned render output.
Accept: The branch has one settled rendering contract, one deterministic backend-neutral projection, a runnable demo observable, and focused evidence. The current anchor, presentation, conformance, and persistence behavior remains green.
-> anchor
-> render-contract
-> render-demo
-> render-evidence
-> render-projection
> Stage owns the canonical selected Worldline and Playback; PresentationHost is platform/execution plumbing.
> Orchestrator is developer-authored ordinary imperative control code inside Stage. It chooses Tau samples, input orchestration, lookahead, branches, persistence, and presentation, but it may not own imperative game state.
> Only publication of a new immutable journal/worldline value may change authoritative game state. InteractionDefinition returns closed Transformation data and cannot construct timestamped journal entries directly.
---
ref [anchor] Completed indexed anchor implementation (build.vine)
The completed anchor supplies the immutable Snapshot, direct query, branches, persistence, presentation boundary, and existing evidence on which this rendering slice depends.
---
[render-contract] Rendering slice contract (notstarted)
Files: proposals/rendering-contract.md
Do: Record the first rendering boundary: immutable `GameState<Snapshot>` plus `Tau` in, owned backend-neutral render value out; exact sampled `LogicalTime` and `Tau` remain observable; tile order and independent terrain, actor, and effect layers remain stable; no frame history or authoritative mutation is admitted. Name the trust boundary of `Renderer` and `Animation` implementations and list the deferred graphics decisions without designing them here.
Accept: One short contract names inputs, outputs, ownership, determinism, stable ordering, and the explicit non-goals. It agrees with the initial specification, semantic contract, productization review, and existing engine-presentation traits.
-> anchor
> The rendering seam remains GameState plus Tau to Frame/render output; rendering does not receive Orchestrator control state or frame history.
> Renderer composition belongs to Stage; backend/device execution remains outside this rendering slice.
